questions.question:
The courier-matcher received OrderPlaced for order `o-88213`, but the order does not exist:

```java
@Transactional
public Order place(PlaceOrder cmd) {
    Order order = orders.save(Order.from(cmd));
    kafka.send("orders.v1", order.id(), new OrderPlaced(order.id()));
    return order;
}
```

```text
10:42:07.118 KafkaProducer  sent orders.v1 key=o-88213 offset=91822
10:42:07.131 SqlExceptionHelper  ERROR: duplicate key value violates unique constraint "orders_idempotency_key"
10:42:07.132 TransactionInterceptor  rolling back order placement
```

Statement: "Kafka accepted the event before PostgreSQL decided at commit, and a rollback cannot recall it; writing the event to an outbox table in the same transaction makes 'the order exists' and 'its event will be sent' one atomic decision."
